  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPROVING THE NUTRITIONAL STATUS OF CHILDREN UNDER FIVE AND WOMEN OF REPRODUCTIVE AGE THROUGH A MULTI-SECTORAL APPROACH IN PUJEHUN DISTRICT - SIERRA L</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to reduce malnutrition in children under 5 by (i) strengthening community and health system&#x2019;s capacities to support the delivery of community based maternal, new born, child and adolescent health and nutrition interventions; (ii) increasing the proportion of pregnant women and caregivers of children under two years who practice key nutrition-relevant behaviours; and (iii) strengthening evidence-based multi-sectoral response to malnutrition. The project will work with communities in eight chiefdoms in Pujehun District which has high rates of acute moderate and severe malnutrition in children under five.</narrative>
  </description>
